## 🔗 Git Branching Strategy (IMPORTANT — All Members Follow This)

| Member | Role | Branch Name | PR Target |
|--------|------|-------------|-----------|
| Member 1 | Full Frontend | `feature/frontend-all` | `main` |
| Member 2 | Backend Core (Auth + Patient APIs) | `feature/backend-core` | `main` |
| Member 3 | Backend Part 2 (Provider APIs + CI/CD) | `feature/backend-provider` | `main` |

```bash
# Every member starts with:
git checkout -b feature/your-branch-name
git push origin feature/your-branch-name
# → When done, open a Pull Request to main
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Never commit `backend/.env`** — only commit [.env.example](file:///d:/Desktop/healthcare%20project/Healthcare-wellness-/backend/.env.example)
> Always pull latest before starting work: `git pull origin main`

