## 👤 Member 3 — Backend Part 2 (Provider APIs + Public Route + CI/CD)

**Branch:** `feature/backend-provider` | **Runs:** `cd backend && npm run dev`

> You build on top of what Member 2 sets up. Import their models and middleware directly. Your job is the provider-facing API, the public health info endpoint, and the CI/CD pipeline.

### Your Responsibilities

#### 1. Provider Routes (`src/routes/providers.js`) — JWT + role=provider
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/provider/patients` | List all patients with compliance badge |
| GET | `/api/provider/patients/:id` | One patient's full goals + reminders |
| GET | `/api/provider/patients/:id/compliance` | Summary: "Goal Met" or "Missed Preventive Checkup" |

**Compliance Logic:**
```js
// Check each patient's reminders:
// Any reminder.status === 'missed'  → badge: "Missed Preventive Checkup" (red)
// All recent reminders  === 'met'   → badge: "Goal Met" (green)
// Otherwise                         → badge: "Upcoming" (blue)
```

#### 2. Public Route (`src/routes/public.js`) — No auth required
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/public/health-info` | Returns static JSON: health tips + privacy policy |

**Sample Response:**
```json
{
  "healthTips": ["Drink 8 glasses of water daily", "Walk 10,000 steps a day"],
  "preventiveCareSchedule": ["Annual blood test (18+)", "Blood pressure check (every 2 years)"],
  "privacyPolicy": "Your data is encrypted and never shared without consent."
}
```

#### 3. Wire Routes into [server.js](file:///d:/Desktop/healthcare%20project/Healthcare-wellness-/backend/src/server.js)
After Member 2 finishes [server.js](file:///d:/Desktop/healthcare%20project/Healthcare-wellness-/backend/src/server.js), add:
```js
const providerRoutes = require('./routes/providers');
const publicRoutes = require('./routes/public');
app.use('/api/provider', providerRoutes);
app.use('/api/public', publicRoutes);
```

#### 4. CI/CD Pipeline — `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
```yaml
name: Healthcare Portal CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [main, "feature/*"]
  pull_request:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  test-backend:
    name: Backend Tests
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with: { node-version: "20" }
      - run: cd backend && npm ci
      - run: cd backend && npm test
        env:
          MONGO_URI: ${{ secrets.MONGO_URI }}
          JWT_SECRET: ${{ secrets.JWT_SECRET }}

  build-frontend:
    name: Frontend Build
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with: { node-version: "20" }
      - run: cd frontend && npm ci
      - run: cd frontend && npm run build
```

**Add GitHub Secrets** (repo Settings → Secrets → Actions):
- `MONGO_URI` — get from Member 2
- `JWT_SECRET` — get from Member 2

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Wait for Member 2 to finish setting up [server.js](file:///d:/Desktop/healthcare%20project/Healthcare-wellness-/backend/src/server.js), all models, and middleware before you start writing routes. You will import `User`, `Goal`, `Reminder` models from Member 2's code.

